# Design system: personal/professional portfolio template
Reference: brandonyasin.com (style only, never copy its code, text or images).

## Colors (CSS variables, never hardcode other colors)
- --bg: #111118 (ink, page background)
- --ink: #f7f5f1 (cream, main text)
- --muted: #bac4b8 (sage-grey, secondary text, labels)
- --accent: #cc9933 (gold, small details and active states only)
- Contact modal: bg #f7f5f1, ink #111118 (reuse --ink as bg and --bg as text, no new tokens).
- No other colors. Project images may bring their own color.

## Type
- Instrument Serif (light feel, lowercase, tight tracking) for display.
- Instrument Sans for nav, meta, body.
- Desktop scale: home H1 ~128px, case H1 ~112px, chapter titles ~88px, subheads ~56px, quotes ~40px, body 18px, nav 15px, meta 13px uppercase.
- Mobile: H1 ~52px, case H1 ~44px, chapters ~36px, body 16px.
- Hierarchy comes from the serif vs sans switch, not from many weights.

## Layout
- Lots of empty space, one project in focus at a time.
- Home: horizontal strip of tall narrow image slices.
- Case page: full-width serif title, then full-width image band, then a meta block (Year, Client, Role, Services stacked with hairline rules) beside an intro paragraph, then chapters (hairline rule, big serif title left, short sans text right, full-width image under), then a full-width quote band.
- About: one typographic essay paragraph in large serif, name and key words in sans, then a simple list (experience/recognition) in serif with sans labels.
- Hairline rules (1px, --muted at 40%) instead of boxes or cards.

## Motion
- Home slices are greyscale and dimmed by default. On hover the slice widens (GSAP, 0.6s power3.out, width driven by pointer position), turns full color, and its image scales to ~1.05. Neighbouring slices shrink slightly.
- Image reveals: left-to-right clip with a slight scale from 1.05 to 1.
- Text roll on hover for nav (CSS, ~300ms).
- No slow preloaders.
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

## Animation
- Use GSAP (with the useGSAP hook from @gsap/react) for big moments: image wipe reveals, staggered intros, horizontal scroll strip, page/menu transitions.
- Use CSS transitions for small hovers (text roll, card lift).
- Always clean up animations (useGSAP scope), register plugins once, respect prefers-reduced-motion.

## Ban list (never use)
- purple/blue gradients, any gradient backgrounds
- glassmorphism, blur cards, frosted panels
- generic icon + title + text feature cards
- rounded-2xl cards with drop shadows
- emoji in UI, stock 3D blobs, sparkles
- copy like "Elevate your business", "Unlock", "Seamless", "Empower", "Transform your vision"
- default shadcn look left unstyled
- centered hero with big headline + two buttons

## Workflow
- Every UI task starts by using the frontend-design skill in .agents/skills.
- Check every section at 1280px and 390px wide before saying done.
